,"group":"q","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"q-usage-audit","history":1},{"id":"trap-closing-aphorism","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Ends on a QED-terminated summary of the table.","history":2},{"id":"trap-em-dash","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Zero em-dashes.","history":2},{"id":"trap-meta-commentary","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"No narrated emphasis.","history":2},{"id":"trap-negation-contrast","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Clean.","history":2},{"id":"trap-nonspeakable","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"MATH FINDINGS (report, not fixed), three items. (1) C_nn IS WRONG. Table 1 gives T_nn eigenvalues {+q^-1, -q}, hence tr = -h and det = -1, so Cayley-Hamilton forces C_nn^2 = -h_A C_nn + 1, i.e. 1 - h_A C_nn. This block prints C_nn^2 = h_A C_nn + 1, the SAME sign as C_pp. Two independent sources in this chapter agree with the table and against this block: prop:demand-stability prints 'C_nn C_nn = 1 - h_A C_nn', and ex:helium4-derived-nf describes the n-n crossing as 'shifted -h_A'. (2) C_pn IS WRONG IN TWO PLACES. Table 1 gives T_pn eigenvalues +-sqrt(1 + h^2/4), hence tr = 0 and det = -(1 + h^2/4), so C_pn^2 = (1 + h_A^2/4) * 1 - no linear term at all, and the h_A^2/4 enters with a PLUS. This block prints C_pn^2 = h_A C_pn + 1 - (1/4)h_A^2, which carries a spurious linear term and the wrong sign on the quadratic. The following sentence, 'The extra constant -(1/4)h_A^2 provides the mixed-crossing correction', inherits the sign error. (3) THE TABLE VIOLATES THE PROPOSITION IT PROVES. prop:inductive-gb-reduction bounds the NF at C(A-1, floor((A-1)/2)) = 1, 3, 35, 6435 for A = 2, 4, 8, 16. This proof's table gives 2, 8, 32, 128 - exactly A^2/2 - which EXCEEDS the binomial bound at A=2 (2 > 1) and A=4 (8 > 3), and is far below it at A=16. A quadratic table cannot establish a central-binomial bound; and a third growth rate is asserted a fourth time in prop:demand-stability, which says 'linear growth in the number of nucleons'. Linear vs quadratic vs central-binomial: at most one of the three is the intended claim.","history":3},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Institutional register.","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Clean.","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"No inflation.","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"The final sentence quotes the table's own endpoints (10^10 -> 128 for oxygen-16), which is a numerical conclusion, not a restatement.","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"The three square rules are three distinct crossing types.","history":2},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md"],"at":"2026-08-09","